# Utils Folder
# 
# Purpose: Store utility functions, helpers, and shared code
# 
# Best Practices:
# - Keep utility functions pure and stateless when possible
# - One utility file per concern (e.g., logger.ts, helpers.ts, validators.ts)
# - Utilities should be reusable across the application
# - Avoid business logic in utilities - keep them generic
# - Export functions individually for better tree-shaking
# - Document utility functions with JSDoc comments
# - Keep utilities focused and small
# - Test utilities thoroughly as they're used across the app
# 
# Example utilities:
# - logger.ts (logging utilities)
# - helpers.ts (general helper functions)
# - validators.ts (validation utilities)
# - formatters.ts (data formatting functions)
# - constants.ts (application constants)

